1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:01,905
If the Sun became a black hole

2
00:00:01,925 --> 00:00:03,847
right now, you wouldn't notice.

3
00:00:03,974 --> 00:00:05,954
For 8 minutes and 20 seconds,

4
00:00:05,974 --> 00:00:07,909
its last light keeps arriving.

5
00:00:07,986 --> 00:00:09,336
Then the Sun just

6
00:00:09,549 --> 00:00:10,511
goes out.

7
00:00:10,771 --> 00:00:11,721
No sunset.

8
00:00:11,806 --> 00:00:12,780
No twilight.

9
00:00:12,800 --> 00:00:14,830
The blue sky is scattered sunlight,

10
00:00:14,850 --> 00:00:16,105
so day turns black,

11
00:00:16,125 --> 00:00:17,781
and stars come out at noon.

12
00:00:17,916 --> 00:00:18,791
Earth's orbit?

13
00:00:18,831 --> 00:00:20,466
Unchanged. Same mass,

14
00:00:20,486 --> 00:00:21,477
same gravity.

15
00:00:21,577 --> 00:00:24,211
The black hole is only 6 km wide.

16
00:00:24,260 --> 00:00:25,440
Through a telescope,

17
00:00:25,460 --> 00:00:27,551
you'd see starlight bending around it.

18
00:00:27,662 --> 00:00:28,742
Then the cold.

19
00:00:28,762 --> 00:00:29,302
In a week,

20
00:00:29,322 --> 00:00:30,802
below −18°C.

21
00:00:30,822 --> 00:00:31,377
In a year,

22
00:00:31,397 --> 00:00:32,656
−73°C.

23
00:00:32,842 --> 00:00:35,017
And Earth keeps orbiting perfectly.

24
00:00:35,067 --> 00:00:36,347
A frozen world,

25
00:00:36,367 --> 00:00:38,374
circling a hole you can't even see.

